sequenceDiagram
  title: Config Resolution — Layer Hierarchy (defaults → file → CLI → ctx)

  participant CLI as main / CLI
  participant DEFAULTS as Config defaults
  participant CFG_LUA as coconut.config.lua
  participant CFG_JSON as coconut.config.json
  participant ARGS as argparse.parse
  participant DARWIN as darwin bundle config
  participant CTX as CoconutContext setters
  participant TBL_MERGE as loadEntryPoint merge
  participant APP as shared Config

  alt config file exists
    CLI ->> CFG_LUA : try coconut.config.lua
    CFG_LUA -->> CLI : parsed Config
  else no .lua
    CLI ->> CFG_JSON : try coconut.config.json
    CFG_JSON -->> CLI : parsed Config — defaults kept on failure
  end

  CLI ->> DEFAULTS : seed window size / title / initial_view / etc.
  DEFAULTS -->> CLI : base layer

  CLI ->> ARGS : --frameless --transparent --title --width --height
  ARGS -->> CLI : CLI overrides beat config-file values

  CLI ->> DARWIN : permissions::applyDarwinConfig(bundle_id, ns.*)
  DARWIN -->> CLI : CFBundleIdentifier + usage descriptions applied

  CLI ->> APP : app::create(&cfg) — Config shared by pointer
  APP -->> CLI : App* with configs = &cfg

  CLI ->> CTX : loadEntryPoint → coconut.config(ctx)
  CTX ->> CTX : setWindowSize / setTitle / setInitialView / setFrameless
  CTX -->> CLI : setters mutate Config in place — app-level overrides

  CLI ->> TBL_MERGE : ret table from coconut.config()
  TBL_MERGE -->> CLI : window_*, initial_view, title, views merged last

  CLI ->> APP : final Config — highest precedence wins per field
  APP -->> CLI : window / lua / bridge modules read the same Config*